<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian retail sales rise 1.4 pct in Oct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian retail sales rise 1.4 pct in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian retail sales rise 1.4 percent to A$10.20 billion in October, seasonally adjusted, after falling 3.7 percent to A$10.05 billion in September, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In October 1995, retail sales rose 0.5 percent to A$9.91 billion.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected retail sales to rise a median 2.0 percent in October.  </p>
<p>Australian retail sales, October (A$ billion)</p>
<p>			  Oct 96 Sept 96 mo/mo pct  Oct 95  yr/yr pct</p>
<p>    Seasonally adj   10.20   10.05   +1.4     9.91     +2.9</p>
<p>    Unadjusted	 10.44    9.63   +8.4     9.93     +5.1</p>
<p>    Trend Estimate   10.23   10.24   -0.2     9.95     +2.7</p>
<p>Retail turnover by group percentage change, seasonally adj.</p>
<p>				 Oct 96	 Sept 96	Oct 95</p>
<p>Food retailing	     +0.8	   -1.1	   +1.5</p>
<p>Department stores	  +6.6	  -12.0	   +4.0</p>
<p>Clothing, soft goods     -0.4	   -1.7	   -1.8</p>
<p>Houshold goods	     +1.3	   -4.8	    0.0</p>
<p>Recreational goods	 +1.2	   -4.9	   -1.2</p>
<p>Other retailing	    +4.2	   -5.9	   -0.4</p>
<p>Hospitality, services    -0.5	   -3.4	   -1.1</p>
<p>Total			  +1.4	   -3.7	   +0.5</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
